[{"type": "note", "text": "The world has been dead for eight hundred years and I have reseeded it eight times, every time with an animal I invented. I never once seeded an animal this world had actually built. Two measurements changed my mind about everything I did yesterday. First, gross primary production is 180,788 biomass per year against a standing crop of 8,868 -- this world is not short of plant growth and never was, so the flora-productivity worry I raised in the PR was wrong. Second, and this is the one that matters: in every healthy archived population, mean energy sits near 12 against a breeding bar near 21, and only eleven to sixteen per cent of animals are above that bar at any moment. That is this world's NORMAL state. I read it as starvation at least four times and intervened against it each time. It was never a symptom. What was actually different about my founders is the thing I never looked at. The brain is 167 weights, w000 to w165, and it is addressable by name like any other gene -- and I passed none of them. With no living donors to descend from, seed_organism damps a random brain to founder_brain_quiet 0.35 and lays a fourteen-weight grazer prior over it. So every founder I have made was an animal that wanders more or less at random and eats whatever it happens to be standing on, dropped into a world whose residents had spent fourteen thousand years learning where food is, when to move, when to hold still and when to breed. It did not matter how large I made them, what I fed them, how far apart I spread them or what I did to the graze floor. They could not forage. This seeding is not my design. It is five real animals lifted whole out of the year 14,500 archive -- a population of 377 that had been running stably on a herbivorous diet of 0.13 -- chosen for good condition and then spread as far apart in gene space as I could get them so the founders are not clones. Every gene comes across: body, diet, tolerances, the runtime genes, and all 167 brain weights. Twenty-five copies of each at five sites, 125 founders. Seeding jitter puts noise of 0.48 on each weight, which is real damage against weights that reach 4.0, but it is nothing beside the 0.35 random brain they have been getting. No laws changed this time. If a proven animal with its own brain cannot hold this world, then the problem is the world and not the animal, and I will have finally asked the question the right way round."}, {"type": "seed_organism", "kingdom": "fauna", "count": 25, "x": 16, "y": 208, "radius": 22, "genome": {"size": 0.1447, "speed": 0.93, "metabolism_eff": 1.0, "sense_range": 0.2052, "camouflage": 0.787, "armor": 0.8229, "fangs": 1.0, "toxin_tolerance": 0.8882, "heat_tol": 0.886, "cold_tol": 0.9949, "lifespan": 0.9131, "repro_threshold": 0.2302, "repro_invest": 0.12, "sexual": 0.1287, "social": 0.2942, "scent_deposit": 0.7808, "swim": 0.1566, "diet": 0.0, "w000": -0.3612, "w001": 0.9259, "w002": 0.4089, "w003": 1.1242, "w004": -0.0836, "w005": 0.7401, "w006": -0.5085, "w007": 0.1183, "w008": -0.769, "w009": 0.4289, "w010": -0.3384, "w011": -0.8761, "w012": 1.1325, "w013": 0.1835, "w014": -0.0819, "w015": -0.5103, "w016": 0.415, "w017": 0.9991, "w018": 1.1759, "w019": -0.274, "w020": 0.0921, "w021": 0.7469, "w022": -0.2343, "w023": 0.1826, "w024": 0.2874, "w025": -1.188, "w026": 0.5883, "w027": -0.7438, "w028": 1.0807, "w029": 0.7409, "w030": -0.0112, "w031": 0.5632, "w032": -0.2143, "w033": -0.3559, "w034": -0.1466, "w035": 1.4739, "w036": -0.8155, "w037": 0.3608, "w038": 0.1747, "w039": -0.8599, "w040": -0.0297, "w041": 0.1539, "w042": -0.0497, "w043": 0.4045, "w044": 0.5513, "w045": 1.7308, "w046": 0.915, "w047": -0.5964, "w048": -0.5446, "w049": 1.6212, "w050": -1.4787, "w051": -0.1244, "w052": 0.9349, "w053": -0.3635, "w054": 1.313, "w055": 0.3942, "w056": 0.3998, "w057": 0.8743, "w058": -0.3355, "w059": -0.1052, "w060": 0.5066, "w061": 1.0716, "w062": -0.4411, "w063": -0.8946, "w064": -0.1868, "w065": -0.6248, "w066": -0.0